============================================================================================
HOW TO READ THIS
============================================================================================
  The FULL row is the entire universe available to a real-time static
  arbitrageur. Without a price for every leg there is no basket sum, so
  there is no deviation to see and nothing to trade -- however fast they
  are. The PARTIAL row is what a model that prices thin legs from their
  neighbours would add.

  A large PARTIAL share is the justification for building the model at
  all: it is not competing with the naive rule, it is reaching a
  population the naive rule cannot reach.

  A small PARTIAL share means the naive rule already sees most of the
  market and the 'just run stat arb' objection largely stands. Report
  the number either way.

  EITHER WAY, quote this next to it: the coverage-extension evaluation
  found the model's estimation error on partially-covered baskets was
  1.49x the signal being detected. Seeing a basket is necessary but not
  sufficient -- pricing it accurately enough to trade is a further step
  this model has not yet cleared.
